---
title: Estimation
summary: Reading a model's least-squares and Fisher-information structure, solving on the host, and stepping on manifolds, the pieces of a damped Gauss–Newton or Fisher-scoring loop.
order: 4
---

Skoro doesn't ship an estimator yet. It ships the pieces one is made from, and those pieces
already compose. This page walks through one iteration of a damped Gauss–Newton / Fisher-scoring
step, top-down.

## The shape of one step

1. **Check coverage.** `require_role(&model, FISHER_ROOT)` guarantees that every scored term offers
   the curvature you are about to use.
2. **Lay out the problem.** `model.tangent_layout(&ids)` fixes the columns (the free quantities'
   tangent coordinates).
3. **Linearize.** `linearize(&model, points, &free, curvature)` builds a block-sparse Gaussian
   factor graph: one factor per term, over only the quantities it reaches. `Curvature::Residual`
   takes each term's `RESIDUAL` rows, $J_t\delta \approx -r_t$; `Curvature::Fisher` takes its
   Fisher root $C_t J_t$ and the gradient of $\log p$. (The dense `jacobian_vjp`,
   `information_root` and `residual_vector` remain for small problems.)
4. **Solve on the host.** Damp with `graph.damped(λ)`, order with a `JunctionTree` (COLAMD, once
   per structure), and `eliminate` by QR into a Bayes tree. `back_substitute` gives the residual
   step at conditioning $\kappa$ rather than $\kappa^2$; `solve_normal(&gradient)` gives the Fisher
   step.
5. **Retract.** `PointMap::retract_flat` applies the step through each quantity's own manifold
   retraction.

The mathematics, and why the Fisher information is the right curvature, is in
[Fisher scoring](../../concepts/fisher-scoring/).

> [!WARNING] Jacobian columns must be leaves
> The columns of `jacobian_vjp`/`jacobian_jvp` are what the estimator moves: `Parameter` and
> `Stochastic` leaves. A mapped node used as a column is rejected with `SkoroError::MappedColumn`.
> Without that check it would come back as a zero column, indistinguishable from a leaf that
> doesn't affect the rows. Derivatives already flow *through* mapped nodes to the leaves. To
> linearize at an interior node, compile with a cut instead (see
> [Compilation](../../concepts/compilation/)).

> [!NOTE] The residual vector
> Nothing yet assembles the residual vector $r$ in the same row order as $J$. A caller evaluates the
> residual nodes and flattens them with the same layout. See [Status](../../reference/status/).

